    "body": "<!-- relay-run-log -->\n**Relay run log** — issue #222\n\n- 2026-09-19 06:06Z — Relay picked up this issue for a BB worker run.\n- 2026-09-19 06:59Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #443 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Pushed branch `bb/relay-222-implementation-audit-fixes-22-23-split-thr_nr5rmtrd3b` to origin. ## Summary Implements issue #222: splits the overloaded `heartbeatFire` task into `heartbeatFireCore` (affinity: `api`) and `heartbeatFireAgent` (affinity: `agents`). - Added `resolveHeartbeatFireTaskName(actionId)` in `scheduler/actions.ts`, resolving `core.agentRun` to the agent task and everything else (all deterministic actions, including library processing) to the core task. - Updated all three enqueue sites — sweep (`sweepDueHeartbeats`), `onItemEvent` trigger (`triggerOnItemEventHeartbeats`), and manual trigger (`createHeartbeatTriggerTool`) — to resolve and dispatch to the correct task name, preserving issue #84's payload/job-key semantics unchanged. - Split `createHeartbeatFireTask` into `createHeartbeatFireCoreTask` / `createHeartbeatFireAgentTask`, both thin wrappers over a shared implementation that now asserts the dispatched action actually belongs on the runtime it was routed to. - Added a one-time install migration (`heartbeatFireQueueSplitMigration.ts`, wired into both `runMigrationsCli.ts` and `testSupport/globalSetup.ts`) that re-enqueues every pending legacy `heartbeatFire` job under the correct new name by resolving its heartbeat's action registration, inside one transaction, with an actionable error and full rollback if a legacy job can't be resolved. New test file covers exactly-once re-enqueue (including the anti-duplication case), agent-vs-core routing, and the unresolvable-heartbeat failure path. - Removed the legacy `heartbeatFire` task name/handler entirely, including the transitional `CORE_TASK_NAMES.HEARTBEAT_FIRE` entry from #221. - `worker.ts`'s single-process test/dev task list registers both new handlers, as required until #91 splits them into separate runners. Both `backend/` and `web/` `pnpm run verify` pipelines pass in full (backend: 1460 integration/unit tests + 9 e2e tests; web: 197 tests), all in the foreground this session. Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-19 07:40Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #443 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Pushed to the existing branch `bb/relay-222-implementation-audit-fixes-22-23-split-thr_nr5rmtrd3b`. ## Summary Addressed the review findings from PR #443's code-review check: **Medium severity (fixed):** - `actions.ts` — replaced the single-entry `AGENT_SESSION_ACTION_IDS` Set with a direct equality check against `CORE_AGENT_RUN_ACTION_ID` (removed speculative generality). - Added direct test coverage in `scheduler.test.ts` for `createHeartbeatFireAgentTask` (payload validation, running the `core.agentRun` handler standalone) and for `assertActionAffinity`'s rejection path in both directions — an agent-session action dispatched to the core task, and a deterministic action dispatched to the agent task — confirming the handler never runs in either mismatch case. **Low severity (fixed):** - `sweep.ts` — `assertActionAffinity` now compares against the `AGENT_TASK_NAMES.HEARTBEAT_FIRE_AGENT` constant instead of a bare string literal. - `heartbeatFireQueueSplitMigration.test.ts` — `getSemprecProjectId` now throws an actionable error instead of an unguarded array-index access when a query returns no rows. Full `backend` and `web` `pnpm run verify` pipelines pass (backend: 1464 integration/unit tests + 9 e2e tests; web: 197 tests), all run and awaited in the foreground this session. Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-19 08:54Z — This issue was resolved by #443, which just merged into develop.",
